1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,716
Welcome to Atomic Education.

2
00:00:02,777 --> 00:00:10,193
This lesson was written by the Atomic teaching team to help you learn Cambridge Lower Secondary Science with confidence.

3
00:00:10,193 --> 00:00:10,929
Let's begin!

4
00:00:11,990 --> 00:00:14,809
Welcome to our final unit, Unit 14: Astronomy.

5
00:00:15,871 --> 00:00:18,506
How did the Moon form? How are stars born?

6
00:00:18,506 --> 00:00:23,471
And what really happened when a huge asteroid struck Earth 66 million years ago?

7
00:00:23,471 --> 00:00:27,393
Scientists even dream of mining asteroids for materials one day.

8
00:00:28,454 --> 00:00:34,583
Asteroids are rocky objects orbiting the Sun, from about 2 metres to nearly 1000 kilometres across.

9
00:00:34,583 --> 00:00:41,019
Most are in the asteroid belt between Mars and Jupiter, but gravity can pull some onto planets and moons.

10
00:00:42,080 --> 00:00:48,393
66 million years ago, a huge asteroid struck the Gulf of Mexico, leaving a crater 200 kilometres wide.

11
00:00:48,393 --> 00:00:53,480
Dust blocked sunlight, so plants couldn't photosynthesise and temperatures dropped.

12
00:00:54,541 --> 00:00:57,912
Most dinosaurs became extinct in this mass extinction,

13
00:00:57,912 --> 00:01:01,835
though small dinosaurs survived and evolved into today's birds.

14
00:01:01,835 --> 00:01:08,147
In 2021, scientists who had drilled into the crater found asteroid dust inside it, confirming the idea.

15
00:01:09,209 --> 00:01:12,763
A tray is filled with flour and dusted with cocoa powder.

16
00:01:12,763 --> 00:01:17,544
The same marble is dropped from 20 centimetres, and then from 80 centimetres.

17
00:01:17,544 --> 00:01:21,589
Predict: which drop will make the bigger crater? Pause and decide.

18
00:01:22,650 --> 00:01:26,879
Watch. From 20 centimetres, the marble makes a small, shallow crater.

19
00:01:27,941 --> 00:01:31,741
From 80 centimetres it hits much faster: the crater is wider,

20
00:01:31,741 --> 00:01:35,295
and white flour is thrown out in long rays over the cocoa.

21
00:01:36,357 --> 00:01:42,424
Explain what you saw. A marble dropped from higher hits faster, so it carries more kinetic energy.

22
00:01:42,424 --> 00:01:47,940
More energy pushes more flour aside, making a wider crater and throwing material further.

23
00:01:47,940 --> 00:01:51,311
A real asteroid travels at many kilometres per second,

24
00:01:51,311 --> 00:01:57,624
so it carries a huge amount of energy: enough to make the Chicxulub crater, about 200 kilometres wide,

25
00:01:57,624 --> 00:02:02,711
and to throw dust high into the atmosphere. Pause and explain it in your own words.
